{
  "_comment": [
    "Source of truth for the Twelve Blooms — Alfheim's native ore family.",
    "tools/gen_blooms.py turns each entry into: an ore block texture+registration, a raw drop",
    "item, a quickened intermediate item, worldgen features, block tags and the Rite recipes.",
    "",
    "Design record: alfheim_reclaimed_design/ORE_SUPPLEMENTATION.md",
    "",
    "Chain shape, per bloom:",
    "  <id>_ore  --mine-->  raw_<id>  --RITE-->  quickened_<id>  --smelt/craft-->  <renders.item>",
    "",
    "'ore'   speckle is extracted by differencing a vanilla ore texture against block/stone.png,",
    "        tinted, and composited over botania:block/livingrock.png — so the blooms read as",
    "        growths in Alfheim's own stone rather than vanilla ore recoloured.",
    "'raw'   and 'quick' tint a vanilla item base; 'quick' also takes a glow overlay.",
    "",
    "'reagents' are Rite I (Petal Apothecary) ingredients alongside the raw drop. Every one is",
    "        verified rooted in Alfheim: petals via the B-46 spawnlist fix, wheat_seeds and",
    "        bone_meal from minecraft:grass placed by mythicbotany:alfheim_grass, #minecraft:saplings",
    "        from the archwood trees in ars_nouveau:placed_mixed_archwoods, wheat from",
    "        mythicbotany:wheat_fields in golden_fields.",
    "",
    "'group' selects the biome modifier. Each bloom appears in EXACTLY ONE group — that",
    "        disjointness is what makes a feature-order cycle impossible from our side (CW-4)."
  ],
  "blooms": [
